NegroniMetal change to metal2vulkan f6a96b7d (+ userland/metal/patches/m2v-flame), applied by scripts/metal/fetch-sources.sh:
no-copy buffers (newBufferWithBytesNoCopy:, IOSurface textures) on a device whose host-pointer imports allow only
host-visible types without HOST_COHERENT (Turnip on Darwin/RedwoodGPU: HOST_CACHED, docs/gpu-abi.md section 6).
- memory.rs: Memory::import_host takes its types from Memory::import_types, which falls back to such types (cached first) where no coherent type is allowed; before
  this the import was refused as Unsupported { HostMemory, NotRepresentable } (no memory type of the class).
- command_buffer/mod.rs: as a command buffer completes, before its status and its completed handlers, it calls
  vkInvalidateMappedMemoryRanges over each such import its commands used (no-copy buffers, buffers under textures,
  no-copy heaps). Turnip (userland/turnip/mesa-patches/0002) passes each to the kernel's CPU_PREP by GEM handle
  (MSM_PREP_NOSYNC), which drops the CPU's lines by physical address; EBUSY (a later submission still lists the buffer)
  is skipped, so a command buffer pipelined after this one on the same import can leave stale lines for a CPU read in
  this one's completed handler. The CPU-to-GPU direction is the kernel's: it cleans CPU-written pages of 0x49 and 0x7e
  imports at each submission that lists them (gpu-abi.md section 6 rule 1).
- buffer.rs: HostPages::import_range (memory, offset, size of the import) for that call.
- tests/negroni_host_import.rs: the type choice for a Turnip-like pointer (cached, not coherent), both the pure
  functions and Memory::import_types of a Memory (fails on a port that puts the fallback outside the import's type choice).
- 2026-10-27 fix for f6a96b7d: the fallback is in Memory::import_host (upstream moved the host import there; the
  first port put it in import_dma_buf, so every no-copy import was refused as HostMemory NotRepresentable).

